{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the S1 compatibility decisions (070231aa)\n\n1. Profile and seed path. S1 uses the current dap-demo cohort (Destination 12) with the explicit J4 profiles issueJ4 and changeJ4 once J4 lands, selected by their pinned digests, and publishes the seed through the retained SDK stage, check and manifest path on Destination 12. It makes no claim that dap propose accepts that cohort; dap propose's support for Destination 12 and the whole-tree change profile is S6's concern (the change view and merge slice), not S1's. No default export changes and no existing room migrates.\n   Seed equality: the expected path set is task-list/ plus the founding README that the destination's initial head carries; the README is not deleted and its bytes are the generator's. The witness compares Git blob bytes for every path, not a tree digest. The pull is a fresh dap clone with a new read token each time, since clone consumes its credential once and no fetch-token command exists; the plan's \"after git pull\" reads as \"after a fresh clone\".\n\n2. Package family. S1 builds no package. It activates the two definitions by the activate act, as room b did, and appends the role actions through the maintained additions route if it is reachable without a package, else through set-actions with the union computed from the retained original lists; the witness retains all five original lists and compares each action after the append. Packaging the repo-in-ai application and choosing its install family is S8 (package and install), which replaces this runbook step. The runbook says so.\n\n3. Checker identity. A genuine native checker: kind checker, role checker, no controller, enrolled by the native add-member checker path with its key enrollment. The two agents are kind agent, role agent, owner as controller, by the tagged agent-key link. If the link helper has no checker mode, S1 adds the smallest one in invitations.ts; no person-with-agent-role substitution, and no agent called a checker. J3's runner joins as that checker.\n\n4. Planner inputs. Owner home ~/.config/generalbusiness/repo-in-ai/owner (a new identity, not the demo operator); agent homes repo-in-ai/agent-a and repo-in-ai/agent-b; checker home repo-in-ai/checker; room label repo-in-ai; the register is dap-demo's (the one room b used). The planner creates the homes and runs the runbook from the builder's command list, as with the J4 rooms; secrets never enter the workroom.\n\n5. Rerun safety. Phase receipts with unknown-stop, retained originals before each send, and a resume that settles a retained original rather than signing a new one, as the J4 packets do. The runbook refuses to continue past an unknown answer without an explicit continue mode.\n\nStill not before J4 lands. Retire this question when read.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}